# As built the closure of `maker` lies in a frame. Under DisableFrameCells, one of the two words of --aot-harden=proof-checks, a build takes the mechanism CellsInFrames away (withoutMechanismsThatOptionsWithhold()).
# testaot's staged commands did not: `walk` laid the cell in a frame, the emitter refused it, and no unit was printed. They ask the same function now: what they print under the word is what a build compiles.
# f2 = maker
# RUN(BUILT): walk f2 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# BUILT-LABEL: code f2:Body
# BUILT: = NewClosure {{*}}storage=Frame
# RUN(KEPT): walk f2 mechanisms=all-Inlining testing=DisableFrameCells
# KEPT-LABEL: code f2:Body
# KEPT: = NewClosure
# KEPT-NOT: storage=Frame
# -- source: main.ts
